# Evaluation keys — values live in the file referenced by GSA_AI_ENV_PATH.
# This file documents the variable NAMES only. Do NOT put secrets here.
#
# The eval harness does NOT use a local .env. Every module reads the
# environment variable GSA_AI_ENV_PATH and loads the .env it points to, so your
# single source of truth stays wherever you already keep it.
#
#   GSA_AI_ENV_PATH=C:\path\to\your\.env
#
# The referenced .env must provide:
#
#   USAI_API_KEY   USAi gateway API key (agent + judges)
#   USAI_BASE_URL  USAi gateway base URL (code appends /api/v1)
#   USAI_MODEL     Default model slug, e.g. claude_4_6_sonnet
#
# Optional overrides (fall back to USAI_MODEL / a sensible default if unset):
#
#   AGENT_MODEL    Model the agent-under-test drives. Default: USAI_MODEL.
#   JUDGE_MODEL    Model the LLM-as-judge uses. Default: claude-sonnet-5.5
#                  (kept distinct from the agent to reduce self-preference bias).
#
# The MCP server under test needs no credentials of its own. For eval runs it
# may optionally reach a running viewer backend via VIEWER_BASE_URL, but the
# viewer does NOT need to be up: tool selection and arguments are what we judge.
